I am submitting this formal complaint regarding Citibank, N.A.s prolonged and unjustified restriction of a U.S. business account, which has now extended beyond fifteen (15) months, and which has escalated into a unilateral account blocked and closure with funds still retained by the bank for an amount about XXXX.
The account was originally restricted due to questions regarding the source of funds. Since the beginning of this process:
All documentation requested by Citibank has been provided immediately and in full, including corporate records, proof of source of funds, tax filings, and repeated verification requests.
The Internal Revenue Service (IRS) has already reviewed the matter, retained applicable taxes, and effectively validated the legitimacy of the funds.
Despite this, Citibank continued to request additional documentation without identifying any unresolved deficiencies or providing a lawful basis for continued restriction.
Citibank representatives repeatedly communicated specific resolution deadlines, all of which were missed without explanation.

In February 2025, Citibank unilaterally closed the account, notifying the account holder only by email, and simultaneously revoked all online access, making it impossible to view balances, transaction history, or account status through Citibanks platform.
Despite the account being closed:
All funds remain retained by Citibank;
No funds have been returned, transferred, or made accessible to the account holder;
No court order, government mandate, or legal hold has been provided to justify the continued retention of funds in a closed account.
To date, Citibank has failed to issue:
A written explanation citing the specific legal or regulatory authority permitting the retention of funds after account closure;
Any documentation indicating that a government agency or court requires the funds to remain frozen.

Citibanks conduct raises serious concerns regarding:
Improper retention of customer funds following account closure;
Failure to provide required transparency regarding legal or regulatory holds;
Unreasonable delay and lack of due process after completion of all requested due diligence;
Misleading communications, including repeated assurances of resolution that were not honored.

We respectfully request that the appropriate regulatory authority review Citibanks actions and require the bank to:
1. Provide a written statement identifying the precise legal or regulatory basis (if any) authorizing the continued retention of funds after account closure;
2. Confirm whether any government agency, court order, or legal hold mandates the restriction;
3. Establish and comply with a definitive and enforceable timeline for resolution;
4. Immediately release the retained funds if no lawful basis exists for continued retention.

Sincerely,\XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX

